                        



Object class: Keter 

Containment measures 

SCP-5133 is to be kept in a tall cell made out of 100% marble. The cell should be at least 25 feet high. Windows and a trapdoor are located at the top, since SCP-5133 cannot climb. For any repairs, the SCP should be stunned with a medium sized bomb (dropped into the cell via trapdoor). SCP-5133 should NEVER be let out of its cell. There is NO EXCEPTION to this rule.

description 

SCP-5133 is a golden colored outdoor hot tub with small legs. It appears to be sentient. The wires on the bottom secrete a oily liquid that is highly corrosive to everything except marble. However, the water inside can corrode through everything lifting the cover. Bombs have shown to stun the SCP for up to a month (depending on the size).

end-of-the-world-scenario 

If ever in contact with the ocean, SCP-5133 will summon a wave and jump to it. The wave will expand at a high rate, eventually crushing everything in its path. Therefore, SCP-5133 is located in ███████, away from the ocean.

discovery 

SCP-5133 was found on a small island where humans lived. The last thing heard from the island before a . Agents soon investigated the area and found SCP-5133 in a small shack.

